node_modules/

# A vault that used to be served from here, and no longer is. NOTHING IS
# WRITTEN BESIDE THE INSTALL any more — the default vault lives in the per-user
# data directory (`dataHome()` in server/workspace/vault.ts) — so this line is
# kept only so an older clone that still has the folder does not start tracking
# a git repo inside this one.
#
# ANCHORED, and the leading slash is load-bearing: an unanchored `workspace/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded
# `server/workspace/` — the whole layer-3 module, 911 lines, never once tracked
# and invisible in every `git status` that should have shown it.
/workspace/

# Where `make up` puts the detached server's log. One machine's running state,
# nothing the repo wants, and `make down` does not clean it up on purpose — the
# log of a server that failed to start is the whole reason to keep it.
.run/

# Which vault was last opened, and the ones before it. It moved to the per-user
# data directory with the default vault — it is about vaults, so it cannot live
# inside one, and it is this machine's rather than this install's, so it cannot
# live beside the program either. Kept here for an older clone that still has it.
.vaults.json

# THE BUILD. `make app` writes all of it: the generated embedded-file manifest,
# the compiled server, the staging directory the Electron bundle is made from,
# and the bundle itself. Generated, large, and per-target — the manifest alone is
# a hundred import lines that change the first time anybody adds a file, which is
# exactly why it is walked rather than written down and why a committed copy
# would be wrong within a day.
/dist/
